course: dictionary
lesson: 11876
title: Short forms and what they stand for
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Br» is not a word you say out loud. It is a fragment, a short piece of a longer word or name, and it only makes sense when you know where you see it.
explain: The same letters can mean different things. «Br» is a chemical symbol in science, and «Br.» can stand for «British», «Brother» or «branch». Look at the subject and the words around it to find the right meaning.
explain: Short forms are common in chat and on screens too. «brb» means «be right back», and the tag «<br>» in web code starts a new line. When you are unsure, think about where you saw it, then check the full form.
fact: «Br» is the chemical symbol for bromine, a dark red liquid element.
fact: «Br.» can be short for «British», «Brother» or «branch».
fact: «brb» means «be right back» in online chat.
fact: In web pages, the tag «<br>» starts a new line.
fact: People almost never say «br» out loud; they say the full word.
exercise: On the periodic table in science, what does «Br» stand for? | A tag that starts a new line | A British person | * The chemical symbol for bromine, a dark red liquid | A brother in a church
exercise: Your friend texts «brb». What does it mean? | Brilliant, really brilliant | Brown and red | * Be right back | Sorry, I am bored
exercise: «Br. John led the prayers.» What does «Br.» most likely stand for? | Break | Bromine | * Brother | Bright
test: In web code, what does the tag «<br>» do? | Adds a picture | Makes the text bold | Plays a sound | * Starts a new line
test: «The branch office opened on Monday.» Which word could «Br.» be short for in a list of offices? | * Branch | Bring | Bright | Bread
exam: Ella sees «Br» in her science book and «Br.» on a letter from her church. What is the difference? | Neither of them is ever used | Br is a brother, and Br. is a liquid | Both mean exactly the same thing | * Br is the symbol for bromine, while Br. is short for a word like British, brother or branch
